From c2ea3f81d888f73bd82c93d3799211011fee3614 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:23:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] boot_main: install the getenv cache only under MSVC

MinGW's CRT import library already defines __imp_getenv (duplicate symbol
at link); there getenv stays the CRT's.
---
 runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp b/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
index 6c9c2eb..f31d125 100644
--- a/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
@@ -166,7 +166,10 @@ char* __cdecl cached_getenv(const char* name)
     return (char*)val;
 }
 }
+#ifdef _MSC_VER
 extern "C" char* (__cdecl* __imp_getenv)(const char*) = cached_getenv;
+#endif  /* MinGW defines __imp_getenv in its CRT import library: the cache is
+         * not installed there and getenv stays the CRT's (slower, correct). */
 
 /* Last-chance crash reporter: vm_base accesses are bounds-guarded, so a real
  * access violation means a HOST pointer deref (e.g. a bad function pointer or a
-- 
